(GRM-11: member_def ::= "To" "do" "the" name "'s" name (("," ("with"|"of"))? params)? "." body "Return" "a" name "," expr "." - the body of a
 manifest member (GRM-10's member_decl). Note the comma before "with"/"of"
 that a plain func_def (GRM-06) doesn't have: `To do the point's 'placed
 at', with ...` - the trailing comma is part of this production, not
 punctuation noise (dropping it is a compile error, not probed here to
 keep this row to the positive case; see THG2 for the negative form).
 Cross-ref THG2-14/THG2-15 (things-b.md), whose probe this one is adapted
 from almost verbatim - the existing ledger already establishes the wider
 claim set (manifest-as-single-source-of-truth, the owner-return rule).
